license: MIT
keywords:
  - digital health
  - assistive AI
  - consent-gated processing
  - medicine reference data
  - deterministic intent routing
  - bilingual software
abstract: >-
  Medora is open-source research software that joins bilingual English and
  Bengali patient-held records and appointment coordination to a consent-gated
  assistive-AI layer of twenty-one endpoints. Its safety properties are
  structural rather than prompt-dependent: external model calls need a
  purpose-specific revocable grant and pass bilingual redaction and
  pseudonymisation, assistant navigation resolves through an immutable
  role-scoped registry that holds no administrative routes, and summary items
  can cite only records the backend supplied. Routing, consent, and red-flag
  detection involve no model. Underneath sits an open Bangladesh medicine
  reference of 7,389 drugs and 67,001 brands, built from five published
  datasets by a single script. Medora is not clinically validated and is not a
  medical device.
